{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.DTBehrendParityObstruction","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.DTBehrendParityObstruction","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Init.Data.Int.Basic","lean:module:Init.Data.List.Basic","lean:module:Init.Omega"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DTBehrendParityObstruction.odd_count_needs_odd_stratum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DTBehrendParityObstruction.odd_count_needs_odd_stratum","kind":"theorem","line":179,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DTBehrendParityObstruction.lean#L179-L187","doc":"**Some stratum must be odd·odd.** Sharpening the parity obstruction, in\ncontrapositive (constructive) form: if *every* stratum contributes an even weighted\nterm `n_i · χ_eu,i`, the count cannot be `3`. Equivalently, any construction supplying\nthe knot DT count must exhibit a stratum carrying **both** an odd Behrend value and\nan odd Euler characteristic. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DTBehrendParityObstruction.dtCount_even_of_all_even","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DTBehrendParityObstruction.dtCount_even_of_all_even","kind":"theorem","line":168,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DTBehrendParityObstruction.lean#L168-L177","doc":"If every stratum contributes an even weighted term, the whole count is even. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DTBehrendParityObstruction.at_least_two_strata","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DTBehrendParityObstruction.at_least_two_strata","kind":"theorem","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DTBehrendParityObstruction.lean#L153-L166","doc":"**At least two Behrend strata.** A stratification with total Euler\ncharacteristic `−2` and Behrend-weighted count `3` cannot have fewer than two\nstrata: the empty one has `χ_eu = 0 ≠ −2`, and a single stratum forces the even\n`n · (−2) = 3`. Hence the supplier of the knot DT count is genuinely singular\n(a smooth moduli has the constant Behrend function `(−1)^dim`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DTBehrendParityObstruction.chiEuTotal_single","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DTBehrendParityObstruction.chiEuTotal_single","kind":"theorem","line":148,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DTBehrendParityObstruction.lean#L148-L151","doc":"The Euler characteristic of a single-stratum stratification is that stratum's\n`chiEuS`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DTBehrendParityObstruction.dtCount_single","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DTBehrendParityObstruction.dtCount_single","kind":"theorem","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DTBehrendParityObstruction.lean#L143-L146","doc":"The weighted count of a single-stratum (i.e. constant-weight) stratification is\n`n · χ_eu`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DTBehrendParityObstruction.chiEu_even_blocks_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DTBehrendParityObstruction.chiEu_even_blocks_three","kind":"theorem","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DTBehrendParityObstruction.lean#L130-L141","doc":"**The obstruction in full generality: every even total is excluded.** For *any*\neven Euler characteristic `E` and any constant Behrend value `c`, the weighted count\n`c · E` is even and so cannot equal the odd target `3`.\n\nThis is why the `−2` vs `−6` ambiguity is harmless: both are even, so the\nconstant-weight class is excluded either way. Only an *odd* total could be rescued\nby a constant weight — and the QOU machinery produces even ones. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DTBehrendParityObstruction.no_constant_weight_yields_three_neg_six","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DTBehrendParityObstruction.no_constant_weight_yields_three_neg_six","kind":"theorem","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DTBehrendParityObstruction.lean#L125-L128","doc":"The same for `−6`, the GGM sandwich `(0,1)` entry — the other integer the G3\ndirective called \"Euler\". Also even, also excluded. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DTBehrendParityObstruction.no_constant_weight_yields_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DTBehrendParityObstruction.no_constant_weight_yields_three","kind":"theorem","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DTBehrendParityObstruction.lean#L118-L123","doc":"**Constant Behrend weight cannot yield the count `3` over `χ_eu = −2`.**\nIf the Behrend function is constant with value `c`, the count is `c · χ_eu = c · (−2)`,\nwhich is even for every integer `c`; the target `3` is odd. This is the parity\nobstruction, stated at its source. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DTBehrendParityObstruction.dtCount","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DTBehrendParityObstruction.dtCount","kind":"def","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DTBehrendParityObstruction.lean#L113-L116","doc":"The Behrend-weighted Donaldson–Thomas count `DT = Σ_i n_i · χ_eu,i`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DTBehrendParityObstruction.chiEuTotal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DTBehrendParityObstruction.chiEuTotal","kind":"def","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DTBehrendParityObstruction.lean#L107-L111","doc":"The unweighted Euler characteristic `χ_eu(M) = Σ χ_eu,i` (Behrend strata partition\nthe moduli, and `χ_eu` is motivic/additive). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DTBehrendParityObstruction.Strata","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DTBehrendParityObstruction.Strata","kind":"def","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DTBehrendParityObstruction.lean#L102-L105","doc":"A Behrend stratification, as the list of its strata: each carries the Behrend\nfunction's constant value `n` on that stratum, paired with that stratum's Euler\ncharacteristic `chiEuS`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}